1
00:03:52,500 --> 00:03:58,500
It's all fun and games until someone raises the dead.

2
00:07:45,000 --> 00:07:51,000
ParaNorman is a family, animation, adventure film directed by Sam Fell.

3
00:11:37,500 --> 00:11:43,500
In the town of Blithe Hollow, Norman Babcock can speak to the dead, but no one
other than his eccentric new friend believes his ability is real.

4
00:15:30,000 --> 00:15:36,000
One day, Norman's eccentric uncle tells him of a ritual he must perform to
protect the town from a curse cast by a witch centuries ago.

5
00:19:22,500 --> 00:19:28,500
Norman Babcock (voice), played by Kodi Smit-McPhee.

6
00:23:15,000 --> 00:23:21,000
Neil Downe (voice), played by Tucker Albrizzi.

7
00:27:07,500 --> 00:27:13,500
Courtney Babcock (voice), played by Anna Kendrick.

8
00:31:00,000 --> 00:31:06,000
Mitch Downe (voice), played by Casey Affleck.

9
00:34:52,500 --> 00:34:58,500
Alvin (voice), played by Christopher Mintz-Plasse.

10
00:38:45,000 --> 00:38:51,000
Sandra Babcock (voice), played by Leslie Mann.

11
00:42:37,500 --> 00:42:43,500
ParaNorman is a 2012 American stop motion animated comedy horror film
directed by Sam Fell and Chris Butler, and written by Butler.

12
00:46:30,000 --> 00:46:36,000
Produced by Laika, the film stars the voices of Kodi Smit-McPhee, Jodelle Ferland, Bernard Hill, Tucker Albrizzi, Anna Kendrick, Casey
Affleck, Christopher Mintz-Plasse, Leslie Mann, Jeff Garlin, Elaine Stritch,  Tempestt Bledsoe, Alex Borstein, and John Goodman.

13
00:50:22,500 --> 00:50:28,500
It is the first stop-motion film to use a 3-D color
printer to create character faces.

14
00:54:15,000 --> 00:54:21,000
In the film, Norman Babcock, a young boy who can communicate with ghosts, is given the
task of ending a 300-year-old witch's curse on his Massachusetts town.

15
00:58:07,500 --> 00:58:13,500
The idea of ParaNorman came from Butler, who thought making such a movie for kids could help express the challenges
kids face growing up, after realizing that zombie films often contained a degree of social commentary.

16
01:02:00,000 --> 01:02:06,000
Production of the stop-motion animation took place at Laika's studio in Hillsboro, Oregon for three years,
with the animating stage of production lasting about two years and beginning in late 2009.

17
01:05:52,500 --> 01:05:58,500
Instead of using traditional 3-D format cameras, the studio had
sixty Canon EOS 5D Mark II DSLR cameras film the movie.

18
01:09:45,000 --> 01:09:51,000
Jon Brion composed the film's musical score.

19
01:13:37,500 --> 01:13:43,500
ParaNorman was released on August 17, 2012, by Focus Features.

20
01:17:30,000 --> 01:17:36,000
It received generally positive reviews from critics, who praised its animation and script, and was
a modest box office success, earning $107 million against a budget of $60 million.

21
01:21:22,500 --> 01:21:28,500
The film was nominated for an Academy Award and a BAFTA for Best Animated Film.

22
01:25:15,000 --> 01:25:21,000
The film explores themes of medium, jock, stop motion, curse, zombie.

23
01:29:07,500 --> 01:29:13,500
The tone is lighthearted.
